@page "/switch/labels"

<div class="demo-section k-form k-form-md k-form-vertical">
    <div class="k-form-field">
        <div class="k-form-field-wrap">
            <TelerikSwitch @bind-Value="@Value"
                           Width="70px"
                           OnLabel="Yes"
                           OffLabel="Nope">
            </TelerikSwitch>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    private bool Value { get; set; }
}

<div class="demo-alert demo-alert-info" role="alert">
    By design, the Switch does not render any labels when the component is styled with the Bootstrap or Material theme.
    To change the default setup and achieve any of the additional predefined layouts, refer to
    <a href="https://docs.telerik.com/blazor-ui/knowledge-base/switch-display-labels-in-bootstrap" target="_blank">this
    knowledge base for showing the labels in Bootstrap and Material</a> or the article on changing the Switch layout
    in the <a href="https://github.com/telerik/kendo-themes/wiki/Change-the-Switch-Layout">kendo-themes</a> Wiki.
</div>
